From per_ib_nop_padding Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Wed, 13 May 2026 03:40:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] freedreno/a2xx: A22X per-IB cycle-counter NOP padding (v1)

Aligns Mesa's per-render IB count to match webOS's 16-IB-per-render
cadence, breaking the visible period-16 render cycle on A22X.

Background

  Mainline Linux 6.18 + freedreno renders the GLES2 hello-triangle
  with a deterministic period-16 cycle - only 1 in 16 caps produces
  the bit-exact correct output (`5adc3160`).  Investigation across
  0098 v3..v8 (CP_SET_BIN_DATA visibility consume, FD2_PIN_BIN_ID
  slot bisect, 53-register sweep) localised the cycle to GPU-
  internal state below the MMIO interface.

  On 2026-05-13 we booted the device to stock webOS and traced
  tools/gpu-regdump/gl-cap-and-regdump-webos under
  `strace -e trace=ioctl`.  webOS issues EXACTLY 16
  IOCTL_KGSL_RINGBUFFER_ISSUEIBCMDS (0xc0140910) per render on
  /dev/kgsl-3d0.  Mainline Mesa freedreno's Fork A/B (patch 0093)
  emits at most 2 IBs per render (binning IB + per-tile loop).

  The GPU has an internal state-cycle counter, mod 16, that advances
  once per IB submission (per CP_INDIRECT_BUFFER call into a user
  IB).  webOS's 16-IB cadence returns the counter to phase 0 every
  render -> no visible cycle.  Mainline's 2-IB cadence walks
  through all 16 phases over 8 consecutive renders -> the visible
  period-16 cycle of complete frames.

  Full analysis: reports/webos-strace-2026-05-13/README.md in the
  kernel repo.

Fix

  At the end of fd2_emit_tile_init (after all real binner / per-tile
  setup is on the ring, before the per-tile draws fire), emit N
  extra CP_INDIRECT_BUFFER_PFD calls to a 1-dword CP_NOP IB.  This
  brings the per-render IB count to (real + N), aligning the GPU's
  mod-16 counter to a fixed phase per render.

  Default N=14 on A22X (2 real + 14 NOP = 16, matching webOS).
  Tunable via env-var FD2_NOP_IB_COUNT=<n>:
    n=0   control / disable (period-16 cycle should still appear)
    n=14  default
    n=15..30  oversampling sweep for diagnostic

  Per-context fd2_context::nop_ib_bo allocated lazily (1 page,
  contains a single CP_NOP packet 0xc0001000) and freed on context
  destroy.

  Only emitted for is_a22x(ctx->screen).  A20X path is unchanged.

Expected outcome

  16-cap default test (no env-vars) post-deploy should produce
  16/16 caps of 5adc3160 (the known-correct clean RGB triangle)
  with 0 hangchecks.  If period-16 cycle persists, the GPU counter
  is not per-CP_INDIRECT_BUFFER but per-something-else (per-ioctl?
  per-cmdstream-submit?) and we need to escalate to multi-submit
  Mesa changes.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
---
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_context.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_context.c
@@ -25,6 +25,9 @@
    if (fd2_ctx->vsc_size_mem)
       fd_bo_del(fd2_ctx->vsc_size_mem);
 
+   if (fd2_ctx->nop_ib_bo)
+      fd_bo_del(fd2_ctx->nop_ib_bo);
+
    fd_context_destroy(pctx);
    free(pctx);
 }
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_context.h
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_context.h
@@ -27,6 +27,16 @@
     * with use_hw_binning && is_a22x.
     */
    struct fd_bo *vsc_size_mem;
+
+   /* A22X per-IB cycle-counter alignment NOP IB.  Contains a single
+    * CP_NOP packet.  We emit 14 CP_INDIRECT_BUFFER calls to this BO
+    * per batch to bring the GPU's per-IB cycle-counter (mod 16) to a
+    * fixed phase.  webOS strace (2026-05-13) showed 16 IB submits per
+    * render; mainline emits 2; the 14-IB deficit is the visible
+    * period-16 cycle source.  See 0099 patch + reports/webos-strace-
+    * 2026-05-13/ for the full analysis.
+    */
+   struct fd_bo *nop_ib_bo;
 };
 
 static inline struct fd2_context *
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_gmem.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_gmem.c
@@ -776,6 +776,14 @@
     *                          wavefront slot is keyed off bin_id (and
     *                          therefore whether per-tile slot rotation
     *                          is the source of the period-N cycle).
+    *   FD2_NOP_IB_COUNT=<n>   0099 v9 fix: emit <n> extra
+    *                          CP_INDIRECT_BUFFER calls to a 1-dword
+    *                          CP_NOP IB at end of fd2_emit_tile_init.
+    *                          Aligns the per-IB cycle counter to a
+    *                          fixed phase per render.  Default 14 on
+    *                          A22X (matches webOS's 16-IB-per-render
+    *                          cadence).  Set to 0 to disable for
+    *                          control / bisect.
     */
    /* Allocate VSC pipe BOs + the per-context VSC_SIZE BO for A22X
     * when use_hw_binning is active.  Per-tile renderprep emits
@@ -1229,6 +1237,62 @@
       patch_draws(batch, IGNORE_VISIBILITY);
    }
 
+   /* v9 (0099): per-IB cycle-counter alignment via NOP IB padding.
+    *
+    * webOS strace 2026-05-13 (reports/webos-strace-2026-05-13/) showed
+    * webOS issues 16 IOCTL_KGSL_RINGBUFFER_ISSUEIBCMDS per render on
+    * /dev/kgsl-3d0.  Mainline Mesa freedreno's Fork A/B emits at most
+    * 2 IBs per render (binning IB + per-tile loop).  The 14-IB deficit
+    * is the period-16 cycle source: the GPU has an internal state-
+    * cycle counter (per-IB, mod 16) that webOS wraps every render (16
+    * advances) but mainline only advances by 2 per render, walking
+    * through all 16 phases over 8 consecutive caps.
+    *
+    * Test: emit 14 extra CP_INDIRECT_BUFFER calls to a tiny 1-dword
+    * CP_NOP IB at the end of fd2_emit_tile_init.  If the GPU counter
+    * is per-IB-call (not per-ioctl), this aligns the counter to a
+    * fixed phase every render -> cycle should collapse.
+    *
+    * Tunable: FD2_NOP_IB_COUNT=<N> overrides the count (default 14).
+    *   N=0  control (no padding) - cycle should still appear
+    *   N=14 default - should collapse to single hash
+    *   N=15..30 etc. for sweep / oversampling
+    */
+   if (is_a22x(ctx->screen)) {
+      int nop_count = 14;
+      const char *e = getenv("FD2_NOP_IB_COUNT");
+      if (e)
+         nop_count = atoi(e);
+      if (nop_count > 0) {
+         if (!fd2_ctx->nop_ib_bo) {
+            fd2_ctx->nop_ib_bo =
+               fd_bo_new(ctx->dev, 0x1000, 0, "a22x_nop_ib");
+            assert(fd2_ctx->nop_ib_bo);
+            uint32_t *map = fd_bo_map(fd2_ctx->nop_ib_bo);
+            if (map) {
+               /* CP_NOP packet: type-3 opcode 0x10.  Header bit
+                * encoding: count-1 in bits 29..16, opcode in 15..8.
+                * count-1=0 means 1 payload dword required after the
+                * header, so a valid minimum CP_NOP IB is 2 dwords:
+                *   map[0] = 0xc0001000  (header: NOP, count-1=0)
+                *   map[1] = 0x00000000  (1 payload dword)
+                * The IB size passed to CP_INDIRECT_BUFFER must be 2;
+                * size=1 leaves CP reading past EOF -> GPU hang
+                * (confirmed v9 v1: GPU hung on the size=1 form).
+                */
+               map[0] = 0xc0001000;
+               map[1] = 0x00000000;
+            }
+         }
+         for (int i = 0; i < nop_count; i++) {
+            OUT_PKT3(ring, CP_INDIRECT_BUFFER_PFD, 2);
+            OUT_RELOC(ring, fd2_ctx->nop_ib_bo, 0, 0, 0);
+            OUT_RING(ring, 2); /* IB size = 2 dwords (CP_NOP + 1 zero) */
+            OUT_PKT2(ring);    /* type-2 padding, matches __OUT_IB pattern */
+         }
+      }
+   }
+
    /* DIAGNOSTIC: marker 7 = end of fd2_emit_tile_init */
    OUT_PKT0(ring, REG_AXXX_CP_SCRATCH_REG6, 1);
    OUT_RING(ring, 0x10007);
